    "scope": "county",
    "scopeKey": "nj/monmouth-county",
    "body": "Monmouth County pricing moves with the shore. Oceanfront and river towns from Sea Bright to Manasquan carry flood-zone rules that have reshaped construction since Sandy — elevated mechanicals, breakaway construction, and pilings all require specialized crews — and historic districts like Ocean Grove add design review on top. Inland, the county shifts to postwar suburbs in Middletown and Marlboro and horse-country custom homes near Colts Neck, each with its own labor profile. Seasonality is real: exterior and shore work compresses into the window between spring and the summer rental season, and demand spikes after coastal storms. Older Victorians in Asbury Park and Red Bank reward contractors who know old framing, and those specialists book up fastest.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n- https://www.njconsumeraffairs.gov/\n- https://www.fema.gov/flood-maps\n\n*Drafted with AI assistance; reviewed by the LicensedList editorial team. Registration or licensure is not an endorsement of a business's competency.*",
