    "scopeKey": "ny/bronx-county",
    "body": "Bronx County work spans two markets. Much of the borough's stock is prewar — Grand Concourse apartment buildings, brick rowhouses in Mott Haven, and attached frames across Fordham and Tremont — where old plaster, aging risers, and shared walls shape interior scopes. Meanwhile City Island, Riverdale, and Throgs Neck offer detached houses, some with genuine driveways, which simplifies staging considerably. Everything files through the NYC Department of Buildings, so design-professional drawings and permit lead times apply as in the rest of the city, and street parking and truck access remain the daily logistical tax on dense blocks. The borough shares the citywide labor pool, and licensed plumbers and electricians book far ahead, while waterfront blocks near Long Island Sound add coastal flood-zone requirements.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n- https://www.nyc.gov/site/dca/index.page\n- https://www.nyc.gov/site/buildings/index.page\n\n*Drafted with AI assistance; reviewed by the LicensedList editorial team. Registration or licensure is not an endorsement of a business's competency.*",
