    "scope": "county",
    "scopeKey": "ny/nassau-county",
    "body": "Nassau County is postwar suburbia at scale, and its pricing dynamics follow. Levitt-era capes and ranches in Levittown, Hicksville, and East Meadow generate a constant stream of dormers, extensions, and kitchen updates — familiar work for local crews, which keeps competition healthy. The complication is jurisdictional: Nassau licenses home improvement contractors through its Office of Consumer Affairs, while dozens of incorporated villages and the towns each run their own building departments, so permit practice varies street by street. South Shore canal and bayfront communities carry flood-zone requirements that add scope to low-lying projects. Demand is intense and steady from the county's dense homeowner base, and the labor market, while large, shares crews with Queens and Suffolk.\n\n---\n**Sources:**\n- https://www.nassaucountyny.gov/\n- https://dos.ny.gov/building-standards-and-codes\n\n*Drafted with AI assistance; reviewed by the LicensedList editorial team. Registration or licensure is not an endorsement of a business's competency.*",
    "author": "LicensedList editorial team",
